Jahshaka patch 0056 — a groupless texture load must not call a null listener.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this. It touches `OgreMain/src/OgreTextureGpuManager.cpp`, which patch
0051 also touches (`reservePoolId`, ~500 lines earlier); the two apply in stack
order.

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325; audit
SPECS/audits/ENGINE_WORKAROUNDS_TO_PATCHES_2026-09-15.md finding F17). Both
texture-load paths — the multiload worker
(`_updateTextureMultiLoadWorkerThread`) and the streaming worker
(`processLoadRequest`) — detect "no archive and no loading listener", log
`"ERROR: Did you call createTexture with a valid resourceGroup?"` at
LML_CRITICAL, and then, two lines later, call
`loadRequest.loadingListener->grouplessResourceLoading( … )` on that null
listener. So the diagnostic upstream wrote for this mistake is followed
immediately by a null-pointer call on a worker thread: the process dies with a
stack nobody can read, and the message that explains it is in the log above the
crash.

Jahshaka met this class of defect through a texture created with `flags 0`
(SSAO's noise texture, 2026-09-08 — "any texture we create and upload ourselves
MUST carry TextureFlags::ManualTexture" is in the workspace CLAUDE.md because of
it). Our own triggers are fixed, and this is the HAZARD, not a workaround we
carry: the next `createTexture` that forgets a resource group should get the
error it already prints.

THE FIX IS THE PATH UPSTREAM ALREADY HAS. Neither site returns early: the
deref is guarded, `data` stays null, and each path then does what it already
does for a file that fails to open or to parse — the multiload worker passes the
request on to the streaming thread ("as if multiload was turned off", its own
comment for the archive-throws case), and the streaming thread substitutes
`mErrorFallbackTexData` (the 2x2 error image) and completes the load. A missing
resource group becomes a logged error and a visible error texture instead of a
process death.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` against the pristine pin and `git apply
--reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane worktree;
`--engine-selftest` byte-identical (`b55e2d5d…`) — no load in the tree reaches
the guarded branch (it is the state the log line calls an error). The
behavioural gate is the importer and asset suites (every from-file texture load)
plus test_engine.

